  "decisions": [
    "Exact SDK v3 slots and interpreter v2 identities include the entire Python build, not only its executable. Existing external/v1/v2 records remain unchanged.",
    "Owner-authenticated installed Python receipts preserve approved immutable builds across catalog omission but refuse explicit withdrawal and identity reuse; their key role cannot authenticate a remote catalog.",
    "One preparation lease/controller serializes SDK and interpreter setup, including cross-operation idempotency and the combined 32-job bound. No setup job selects/enables CIGAR.",
    "The native owner alone derives paths/origins/hashes. Explicit operator imports and native downloads share exact archive verification; browser inputs are opaque IDs only.",
    "Each new owner process reads the complete Python tree. Process-local metadata rechecks are restricted to same-device APFS nanosecond change times; unknown/coarse filesystems keep full-byte verification.",
    "The cache cannot be deserialized, persisted as approval, or rebound. Metadata checks include all files/directories, ctime, inode, permissions, owner and link count; restored length/mtime does not revive modified code.",
    "Publication flushes file modes and parent directory entries. Lost replies reconcile actual authenticated records/bytes without replaying probes. Cleanup retains ownership through bounded partial work and preserves registered references.",
    "The same production native reader now distinguishes bounded atomic replacement retries from persistent invalid/private-file failures; neither class grants readiness."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Bundled SDK and Python entries remain upstream_only; test catalog keys are not production trust roots or qualification promotion.",
    "The real private interpreter workflow imports its exact archive offline. Native Astral download routing is implemented and refusal-tested but still needs its own live download qualification.",
    "The current-runtime continuity fixture uses explicitly enrolled final0.14.1 on CPython3.14.7, not original b47380 bytes or a newer SDK version. No real newer CIGAR release upgrade is claimed.",
    "Only local macOS arm64/APFS source execution is measured. Other platforms, installed/frozen packages, broader approval/performance matrices and all context crate real-runtime tests need final P9/P10 execution.",
    "Complete CLI/HTTP/UI, discovery, maintenance/pruning, qualification refresh/historical reuse, exact preview/core label handling, data preflight/copy generations, serialized switch/rollback and catalog/withdrawal cache remain unfinished.",
    "Production catalog hosting and authorized signing roots are unresolved; no feed, signer or downloaded adapter was invented.",
    "Rust1.99 global rustfmt differs on one untouched inventory-contract test import; the repository/CI-pinned Rust1.88 full formatting check passes without unrelated edits."
  ],
